text.section:
Training centers shall employ only motorcycle safety instructors who meet the following minimum qualifications:

Have a current, valid driver's license, endorsed for motorcycle operation, that is neither suspended, revoked, cancelled, nor under probation, with less than six demerit points in a 12-month period and no conviction for any of the offenses enumerated in subsection E of § 18.2-270;


Be a valid training course instructor, as approved by the Department, which includes:
				a. Having instructor certification to teach the current curriculum approved by the Department;
				b. Attending all required program clinics offered by the Department that provide continuously updated course instructor and motorcycle safety education; and
				c. Avoiding putting course participants or others associated with course instruction in physical danger during periods of instruction through the use of appropriate instruction techniques and methods;


Conduct themselves in a professional manner, including, but not limited to, using appropriate language and having interactions with participants and others involved in the course that are free from threat and intimidation; and


Comply with other requirements specified in this article.
